## Standard Branches

Enterprise mobile repositories utilize a standardized multi-branch topology:

<div class="portal-table-wrap">
  <table class="portal-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Branch Name</th>
        <th>Branch Role &amp; Purpose</th>
        <th>Access Rules</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>master</code> / <code>prod</code></td>
        <td><strong>Production-ready code.</strong> Reflects live App Store and Google Play releases.</td>
        <td>Strictly protected. Merges only via Release or Hotfix PRs. Direct pushes blocked.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>develop</code></td>
        <td><strong>Active development and sprint integration.</strong> Target branch for completed features.</td>
        <td>Protected. Merges only via approved Feature PRs. CI runs on every commit.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>user_testing</code></td>
        <td><strong>UAT, QA staging, and stakeholder validation.</strong> Builds distributed to internal testers.</td>
        <td>Automated CI deployment triggers test builds via Firebase App Distribution / TestFlight.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>feature-*</code></td>
        <td><strong>New features and enhancements.</strong> Created by engineers for sprint tasks.</td>
        <td>Branch owner pushes. Short-lived; merged into <code>develop</code> via PR.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>bugfix-*</code></td>
        <td><strong>Bug fixes.</strong> Non-critical bug repairs identified during sprint development.</td>
        <td>Branched from and merged back into <code>develop</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>hotfix-*</code></td>
        <td><strong>Emergency production fixes.</strong> Urgent patches for live production bugs.</td>
        <td>Branched from <code>master</code>. Merged into <strong>both</strong> <code>master</code> and <code>develop</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>release-*</code></td>
        <td><strong>Release preparation and validation.</strong> Feature freeze, version bumps, release notes.</td>
        <td>Branched from <code>develop</code>. Merged into <code>master</code> and <code>develop</code>.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

