## Feature Branch Workflow

### 1. Create a Feature Branch
Always start your work from the latest updated `develop` branch:

```bash
# 1. Switch to develop
git checkout develop

# 2. Prune remote references and pull latest commits
git fetch -p origin
git pull origin develop

# 3. Create and switch to your feature branch
git checkout -b feature-123-add-azure-authentication
```

### 2. Branch Naming Conventions
Branch names must be lowercase, hyphen-separated, and include the Jira ticket key where applicable:

<div class="portal-table-wrap">
  <table class="portal-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Branch Pattern</th>
        <th>Example Branch Name</th>
        <th>When to Use</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>feature-[ticket]-[description]</code></td>
        <td><code>feature-123-add-azure-authentication</code></td>
        <td>New feature work associated with a Jira ticket.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>feature-[description]</code></td>
        <td><code>feature-user-profile-screen</code></td>
        <td>Un-ticketed or cross-cutting feature enhancement.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>bugfix-[description]</code></td>
        <td><code>bugfix-login-crash</code></td>
        <td>Sprint-level defect resolution in development.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>hotfix-[description]</code></td>
        <td><code>hotfix-payment-timeout</code></td>
        <td>Urgent production issue requiring immediate release.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>release-[version]</code></td>
        <td><code>release-2026.10</code></td>
        <td>Sprint release candidate branch.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

### 3. Best Practices for Feature Branches
* **One feature per branch:** Keep branch scope tight. Do not mix unrelated refactors with new feature work.
* **Keep branches short-lived:** Aim to merge branches within 2 to 3 days to prevent large merge conflicts.
* **Commit frequently:** Make small, logical commits with clear Conventional Commit messages.
* **Sync regularly with `develop`:** Rebase or merge `develop` daily to catch integration issues early.
* **Use meaningful branch names:** Describe the technical goal clearly in the branch identifier.

