## Forking a Repository

While internal feature development takes place within the central repository using feature branches, **forking** is utilized for cross-organization contributions and external contractor engagements.

### When Forking is Useful:
* Working with external contributors or third-party vendors.
* Contributors do not have direct write access to the primary repository.
* Experimenting with proof-of-concept architectures independently.

### Keeping Your Fork Updated:
Keep your local clone synchronized with the upstream enterprise repository:

```bash
# 1. Add upstream enterprise repository
git remote add upstream https://github.enterprise.internal/mobile/enterprise-app.git

# 2. Fetch upstream branches
git fetch upstream

# 3. Switch to your local main branch
git checkout main

# 4. Merge upstream updates into your fork
git merge upstream/main
```

